# Git applies the LAST matching pattern for a given attribute, so the general rule comes
# first and the exceptions follow it.

# Normalise text in the repository, check out CRLF: this is a Windows PowerShell project.
* text=auto eol=crlf

*.png binary

# Never touch the vendored community scripts. They are Authenticode-signed by Andrew S Taylor
# and redistributed byte-for-byte; any line-ending translation invalidates both the signature
# and the SHA256 recorded in vendor/VERSION.json, which build.ps1 and Test-ApVendorScript
# both verify. -diff also keeps these 200 KB of signed script out of diffs.
vendor/*.ps1 -text -diff

# Generated single-file build. Treated as binary for diff purposes only: it is ~535 KB and
# largely base64, so a textual diff is noise. Line endings still normalise, which is safe
# because the embedded signed payloads are base64 and decoded back to exact bytes at runtime.
dist/*.ps1 -diff
